Five templates: Timeline, Timeline item, Timeline event, Timeline parallel, Timeline gap (names are placeholders; see Docs.md on renaming). Put the styles in <code>Template:Timeline/styles.css</code>, copied from <code>prototype/timeline.css</code>.
Needs <code>#if</code> (ParserFunctions). Do not leave blank lines between items or events: wikitext turns them into stray paragraphs inside the list.

== Simple: one event per dot ==
<pre>
{{Timeline
|{{Timeline item |date=1612 |title=The Go academy |text=The Tokugawa shogunate patronises the game.}}
{{Timeline item |date=c. 1651 |title=Huang Longshi |text=Born. |image=Huang Longshi.jpg |caption=Huang Longshi}}
{{Timeline item |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo defeats Lee Sedol}}
}}
</pre>

== Several events on one dot ==
<pre>
{{Timeline
|{{Timeline item |date=2006 |events=
{{Timeline event |title=Crazy Stone |text=Monte Carlo tree search arrives in Go.}}
{{Timeline event |title=UCT |text=The UCT algorithm is published.}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Compact variant ==
Add <code>compact=yes</code> for a dense list: one row per date, a solid bar instead of a rail with dots. Good for long release or year-by-year lists. An item may have no events (only a <code>date</code>), which gives an empty bar segment. Not meant for use inside <code>Timeline parallel</code>.
<pre>
{{Timeline |compact=yes
|{{Timeline item |date=1994 |title=Arena}}
{{Timeline item |date=1995}}
{{Timeline item |date=2002 |events=
{{Timeline event |title=Morrowind}}
{{Timeline event |title=Tribunal}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Nested timelines ==
Give an item a <code>sub</code> parameter holding more <code>Timeline item</code>s. They appear indented under that item, with their own rail, and can nest further. Do not indent the wikitext lines with spaces (that makes a preformatted block); the indentation is in the rendering.
<pre>
{{Timeline
|{{Timeline item |date=1990s |title=Neural networks meet Go |sub=
{{Timeline item |date=1994 |title=NeuroGo}}
{{Timeline item |date=1996 |title=Golem}}
}}
{{Timeline item |date=2016 |title=AlphaGo}}
}}
</pre>

== Parallel timelines (several timelines on one row) ==
Wrap timelines in <code>Timeline parallel</code> and give each a <code>title</code>. They share the row and wrap onto the next one when there is no horizontal space. Each keeps its own dates and rail; nothing lines up across them. Inside a row the timelines always use the compact layout (date above the events).
<pre>
{{Timeline parallel
|{{Timeline |title=Players
|{{Timeline item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{Timeline item |date=November 2019 |title=Lee Sedol retires}}
}}
{{Timeline |title=Programs
|{{Timeline item |date=1968 |title=First Go program}}
{{Timeline item |date=2006 |events=
{{Timeline event |title=Crazy Stone}}
{{Timeline event |title=UCT}}
}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Parallel and grouped timelines (dots aligned) ==
Add <code>grouped=yes</code>. At 640 px and wider the n-th item of every timeline then sits on the same row, so dots line up horizontally. To skip a row in one timeline, put <code>{{Timeline gap}}</code> in its place. Rules: every timeline needs a <code>title</code>; at most 20 items (including gaps) per timeline; do not end a timeline with gaps. The columns share the width and do not wrap; below 640 px the timelines fall back to the independent, wrapping layout.
<pre>
{{Timeline parallel |grouped=yes
|{{Timeline |title=Players
|{{Timeline item |date=1846 |title=The Ear-Reddening Game}}
{{Timeline gap}}
{{Timeline item |date=March 2016 |title=Lee Sedol wins game 4}}
}}
{{Timeline |title=Programs
|{{Timeline gap}}
{{Timeline item |date=1968 |title=First Go program}}
{{Timeline item |date=March 2016 |title=AlphaGo wins the match}}
}}
}}
</pre>

== Parameters ==
; Timeline parallel: <code>1</code> timelines; <code>grouped</code> (set to anything to align dots).
; Timeline: <code>1</code> items; <code>compact</code> (set to anything for the dense variant); <code>title</code> (optional heading; use it inside a row).
; Timeline item: <code>date</code>; either <code>title</code>, <code>text</code>, <code>image</code>, <code>imagesize</code>, <code>imagealt</code>, <code>caption</code> (one event) or <code>events</code> (several <code>Timeline event</code>); optional <code>sub</code> (nested <code>Timeline item</code>s).
; Timeline event: same fields as the one-event shorthand.
; Timeline gap: no parameters.
